WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:11.450 --> 00:00:15.430
King Leopold II ruled over Belgium from 1865
to 1909.

00:00:15.430 --> 00:00:20.439
Today, the memory of his reign still lives
on, and he is glorified with golden statues

00:00:20.439 --> 00:00:23.980
of his likeness in every major city in Belgium.

00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:28.310
In history classes, each generation is taught
that he was a humanitarian who brought Christianity

00:00:28.310 --> 00:00:31.090
and the wonders of civilization to The Congo
Free State.

00:00:31.090 --> 00:00:34.510
However, the truth has been kept away from
the Belgian people.

00:00:34.510 --> 00:00:40.310
The reality is that King Leopold II is responsible
for the murder and mutilation of 10 million

00:00:40.310 --> 00:00:41.400
Congolese people.

00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:48.490
This just may be the biggest cover-up in European
history.

00:00:48.490 --> 00:01:02.310
Early and Personal Life
Leopold II was born in 1835 to King Leopold

00:01:02.310 --> 00:01:04.739
I and Louise-Marie of Orleans.

00:01:04.739 --> 00:01:08.960
They were the very first royal family of Belgium,
because the country was just 5 years old.

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:13.050
For thousands of years, that territory had
been conquered by nearby Netherlands, France,

00:01:13.050 --> 00:01:14.470
Germany, and Luxembourg.

00:01:14.470 --> 00:01:19.320
They were a newly independent country that
had yet to form a unique national identity.

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:22.819
Leopold II had two younger siblings called
Phillipe and Charlotte.

00:01:22.819 --> 00:01:26.439
Their family life was dysfunctional, to say
the least.

00:01:26.439 --> 00:01:32.329
Soon after Charlotte’s birth, in 1844, King
Leopold I met a 16-year old girl named Arcadie

00:01:32.329 --> 00:01:33.329
Claret.

00:01:33.329 --> 00:01:37.210
He was 54 years old at the time, but that
didn’t stop him from having an affair with

00:01:37.210 --> 00:01:38.280
a teenage girl.

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:42.670
Claret would go on to become a Baroness, and
her sons, Georg and Arthur, were made into

00:01:42.670 --> 00:01:43.670
Barons.

00:01:43.670 --> 00:01:48.490
There were rumors that Leopold I had several
other affairs, so the exact number of half-siblings

00:01:48.490 --> 00:01:51.350
Leopold II has out there is actually unknown.

00:01:51.350 --> 00:01:55.670
Queen Louise-Marie was understandably miserable
in her marriage, and she chose to let out

00:01:55.670 --> 00:01:57.280
her anger on her children.

00:01:57.280 --> 00:02:01.700
She would make fun of young Leopold II’s
large nose that he inherited from his father.

00:02:01.700 --> 00:02:06.789
She told her son that his face was “disfigured’,
and that he had the beak of a bird.

00:02:06.789 --> 00:02:12.030
In 1853, when he was 18 years old, Leopold
II had an arranged marriage with Marie Henriette

00:02:12.030 --> 00:02:13.030
of Austria.

00:02:13.030 --> 00:02:17.830
Since he had never actually seen what a loving
marriage looks like, the teen couple was incredibly

00:02:17.830 --> 00:02:19.330
awkward around one another.

00:02:19.330 --> 00:02:22.939
Someone in the Belgian royal court had commented
that seeing them together was like watching

00:02:22.939 --> 00:02:24.799
a “nun and a stable boy”.

00:02:24.799 --> 00:02:29.470
People thought that this was so hilariously
accurate, the phrase was repeated amongst

00:02:29.470 --> 00:02:30.920
everyone who knew them.

00:02:30.920 --> 00:02:35.300
Apparently, his parents cared so little about
Leopold, that they never even bothered to

00:02:35.300 --> 00:02:37.129
tell him about the birds and the bees.

00:02:37.129 --> 00:02:41.850
Leopold’s aunt, Queen Victoria of England,
had a great marriage with her husband Albert,

00:02:41.850 --> 00:02:45.689
and she apparently gave her nephew a lot of
sex advice...

00:02:45.689 --> 00:02:49.530
Which was probably exactly as awkward as you
might imagine.

00:02:49.530 --> 00:02:54.190
Leopold II and Marie Henriette eventually
figured it out, because they had two daughters

00:02:54.190 --> 00:02:55.190
together.

00:02:55.190 --> 00:03:01.150
When Leopold I died in 1865, Leopold II ascended
the throne as the new King of Belgium.

00:03:01.150 --> 00:03:05.120
Since his personal life was so dysfunctional,
it’s really no surprise that his happiness

00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:08.569
and satisfaction came from attaining material
things.

00:03:08.569 --> 00:03:13.379
According to William II, the ruler of Germany,
he was together watching a parade with Leopold

00:03:13.379 --> 00:03:18.530
II in Berlin, when he commented, “There
is really nothing left for us kings except

00:03:18.530 --> 00:03:19.530
money.”

00:03:19.530 --> 00:03:27.430
Building His Fortune
Before he died, King Leopold II’s father

00:03:27.430 --> 00:03:32.610
made 50 attempts to conquer a colony for Belgium,
but he had always failed.

00:03:32.610 --> 00:03:36.499
It was clear to him that the power other countries
like England, France, Germany, and the United

00:03:36.499 --> 00:03:38.870
States had was thanks to colonization.

00:03:38.870 --> 00:03:43.510
Leopold I believed that without colonizing
an African nation, they would never be considered

00:03:43.510 --> 00:03:45.860
one of the larger world powers.

00:03:45.860 --> 00:03:49.670
Leopold II picked up where his father left
off, but he did not want to conquer a nation

00:03:49.670 --> 00:03:51.040
on behalf of Belgium.

00:03:51.040 --> 00:03:55.060
He planned to make an entire country his personal
property, instead.

00:03:55.060 --> 00:03:59.109
This way, he could have complete control,
and have direct access to the profits.

00:03:59.109 --> 00:04:03.549
He knew that if he was honest about his greedy
intentions, none of the other major powers

00:04:03.549 --> 00:04:07.359
would agree to let him colonize an entire
country all for himself.

00:04:07.359 --> 00:04:12.159
So, he told everyone that it was his mission
to spread Christianity in The Congo.

00:04:12.159 --> 00:04:17.170
He wanted to convert and civilize those poor,
Godless souls.

00:04:17.170 --> 00:04:21.829
In 1884, he met with 14 other European nations
at The Berlin Conference.

00:04:21.829 --> 00:04:25.580
He pitched his idea for colonizing the Congo,
and claimed that he wanted to spend his own

00:04:25.580 --> 00:04:30.640
fortune to bring missionaries to Africa out
of the goodness of his own heart.

00:04:30.640 --> 00:04:35.290
He also promised that the rest of Europe could
freely explore and trade from his country

00:04:35.290 --> 00:04:36.290
as they pleased.

00:04:36.290 --> 00:04:39.370
The Congo was known for being incredibly dangerous,
and difficult to colonize.

00:04:39.370 --> 00:04:43.940
The rainforest and savannah are filled with
gorillas, lions, leopards, and wolves.

00:04:43.940 --> 00:04:49.260
The Congo River has man-eating crocodiles
and hippopotamus, and insects carry deadly

00:04:49.260 --> 00:04:50.260
diseases.

00:04:50.260 --> 00:04:55.060
In general, it was a very wild place, and
not many Europeans wanted to live there.

00:04:55.060 --> 00:04:57.990
If Leopold II really wanted to take on the
challenge, the other world powers didn’t

00:04:57.990 --> 00:05:00.160
see anything wrong with it.

00:05:00.160 --> 00:05:05.240
A Welsh explorer and journalist named Henry
Morton Stanley already had years of experience

00:05:05.240 --> 00:05:06.240
in Africa.

00:05:06.240 --> 00:05:10.710
He was sent on projects by several different
newspapers in the United Kingdom, and he became

00:05:10.710 --> 00:05:12.560
an expert on the continent.

00:05:12.560 --> 00:05:17.410
Through his writing, he tried to convince
Queen Victoria that despite all of the difficulty,

00:05:17.410 --> 00:05:21.150
he believed it would be worthwhile to colonize
the Congo.

00:05:21.150 --> 00:05:26.770
His suggestions never made any impact, until
King Leopold II found Stanley’s work.

00:05:26.770 --> 00:05:30.970
In 1879, the king sent him on a mission to
colonize the Congo.

00:05:30.970 --> 00:05:35.380
Henry Morton Stanley used parlor tricks to
convince the African tribal chiefs that white

00:05:35.380 --> 00:05:36.840
men were invincible.

00:05:36.840 --> 00:05:42.570
He used a battery-powered contraption to make
his grip so strong, Congolese men almost collapsed

00:05:42.570 --> 00:05:44.650
from a mere handshake.

00:05:44.650 --> 00:05:49.310
Stanley claimed that white men could rip a
tree out of the ground with his bare hands.

00:05:49.310 --> 00:05:54.300
He held a magnifying glass in the sunlight
and used its reflection to light his cigar,

00:05:54.300 --> 00:05:57.340
claiming that white men had power over the
sun.

00:05:57.340 --> 00:05:59.670
Finally, he handed a gun to a native man.

00:05:59.670 --> 00:06:03.430
He instructed him to step back several yards,
and try to shoot him.

00:06:03.430 --> 00:06:07.060
Stanley had taken the gunpowder and bullet
out beforehand, of course, and when the young

00:06:07.060 --> 00:06:11.310
man pulled the trigger, Stanley would double
over dramatically, only to take his shoe off

00:06:11.310 --> 00:06:13.850
and shake the bullet onto the ground.

00:06:13.850 --> 00:06:17.950
He claimed that white men were spirits who
could not be killed, no matter how hard they

00:06:17.950 --> 00:06:21.260
tried, and that a bullet would pass right
through them.

00:06:21.260 --> 00:06:25.320
This was enough to terrify the chiefs into
signing his contract that declared King Leopold

00:06:25.320 --> 00:06:27.350
II as the new owner of The Congo.

00:06:27.350 --> 00:06:31.850
Of course, the Congolese people had no idea
what the contract actually said, but it served

00:06:31.850 --> 00:06:35.320
as a legal document in the eyes of European
people.

00:06:35.320 --> 00:06:38.210
Leopold wanted to keep up the illusion that
he was going to do good in the country, so

00:06:38.210 --> 00:06:41.070
he went as far as to name it “The Congo
Free State”.

00:06:41.070 --> 00:06:45.070
Henry Morton Stanley published a book about
his journey through Africa called Through

00:06:45.070 --> 00:06:46.210
the Dark Continent.

00:06:46.210 --> 00:06:51.440
He was able to go on a lecture tour around
London, and he was even knighted in the year

00:06:51.440 --> 00:06:52.900
1899.

00:06:52.900 --> 00:06:59.690
Colonization and Exploitation
Leopold II truly was paying for all of the

00:06:59.690 --> 00:07:03.370
startup expenses to colonize The Congo out
of his own pocket.

00:07:03.370 --> 00:07:07.030
He appointed governor generals to manage the
various territories of the country.

00:07:07.030 --> 00:07:11.850
Leopold’s men eventually discovered that
the rainforest had a plentiful supply of rubber

00:07:11.850 --> 00:07:12.850
trees.

00:07:12.850 --> 00:07:15.380
This was like stumbling across a gold mine.

00:07:15.380 --> 00:07:19.370
At the time, there was a huge demand for natural
rubber in order to make tires, but there was

00:07:19.370 --> 00:07:21.320
a very small supply.

00:07:21.320 --> 00:07:25.710
The only problem, of course, was finding a
way to pay for manual labor.

00:07:25.710 --> 00:07:30.850
Leopold II ordered his men to enslave the
Congolese people.

00:07:30.850 --> 00:07:33.910
Each of the governor generals had their own
tactic to achieve this.

00:07:33.910 --> 00:07:37.910
Usually, they set a village on fire, so that
there was nowhere for anyone to hide.

00:07:37.910 --> 00:07:41.340
They would shoot and capture the women of
the village, and tell the men that if they

00:07:41.340 --> 00:07:45.650
did not each bring back 15kg of rubber by
the end of the day, they would kill their

00:07:45.650 --> 00:07:46.950
wives and daughters.

00:07:46.950 --> 00:07:50.250
The Congo Free State was anything but free.

00:07:50.250 --> 00:07:54.160
King Leopold II believed that all of these
people were his personal slaves, and he could

00:07:54.160 --> 00:07:56.100
do whatever he wanted with them.

00:07:56.100 --> 00:08:00.360
King Leopold personally handed out bonuses
to the commanders if they could produce more

00:08:00.360 --> 00:08:02.880
rubber, by any means necessary.

00:08:02.880 --> 00:08:07.080
Leopold began to grow his own private army
in the Congo called The Force Publique.

00:08:07.080 --> 00:08:11.520
When his men were destroying a village, they
would pick out the tallest and strongest-looking

00:08:11.520 --> 00:08:13.090
young men to recruit them as soldiers.

00:08:13.090 --> 00:08:17.550
These captured soldiers were instructed to
systematically kill anyone who disobeyed the

00:08:17.550 --> 00:08:19.350
orders of the governor generals.

00:08:19.350 --> 00:08:21.680
They were told that they were not allowed
to waste any ammunition, and that they must

00:08:21.680 --> 00:08:23.970
kill a man with a single bullet.

00:08:23.970 --> 00:08:27.730
They were required to bring back one severed
hand for every bullet fired.

00:08:27.730 --> 00:08:30.580
If they did not, they would be killed by their
general.

00:08:30.580 --> 00:08:34.279
This lead to the soldiers cutting the hands
off of people that were still alive, whenever

00:08:34.279 --> 00:08:35.320
they wasted ammunition.

00:08:35.320 --> 00:08:38.820
Meanwhile, in Europe, people had no idea what
was actually going on.

00:08:38.820 --> 00:08:42.409
Word got around that King Leopold II needed
more soldiers to help with his “Christian

00:08:42.409 --> 00:08:44.450
mission” to colonize The Congo.

00:08:44.450 --> 00:08:48.950
Hundreds of young men from Belgium, Italy,
Norway, Sweden, and Denmark all signed up

00:08:48.950 --> 00:08:50.420
to join The Force Publique.

00:08:50.420 --> 00:08:54.330
They were taught that these black natives
were animals, and not fully human like them,

00:08:54.330 --> 00:08:57.230
so they shouldn’t feel guilty about killing
them when necessary.

00:08:57.230 --> 00:09:01.260
After a while, these men became desensitized
to the killing.

00:09:01.260 --> 00:09:05.050
Some of the soldiers would gut people and
pull out their entrails, or slice off a group

00:09:05.050 --> 00:09:08.090
of men’s genitalia only to hang them in
a row.

00:09:08.090 --> 00:09:11.730
Some of the governor generals wrote letters
to King Leopold II about these scenes, because

00:09:11.730 --> 00:09:14.870
they were actually proud of the brutality.

00:09:14.870 --> 00:09:18.740
They believed that the worse they treated
the Congolese people, the harder they worked.

00:09:18.740 --> 00:09:24.310
Over time, King Leopold’s men managed to
enslave the entire population of the Congo.

00:09:24.310 --> 00:09:27.060
Even though he had promised that the rest
of the world could visit The Congo whenever

00:09:27.060 --> 00:09:32.560
they wanted, King Leopold II became very nervous
when he learned that Arabian merchants were

00:09:32.560 --> 00:09:34.460
coming to gather some rubber for themselves.

00:09:34.460 --> 00:09:38.580
He did not want to lose his monopoly over
the industry, so he declared that they needed

00:09:38.580 --> 00:09:43.150
to go to war with these so-called “Arab
slave traders”, in order to “free” his

00:09:43.150 --> 00:09:44.150
Congolese people.

00:09:44.150 --> 00:09:47.060
This sparked the two year Congo-Arab War.

00:09:47.060 --> 00:09:51.220
In 1895, an English merchant named Charles
Stokes was on a mission for the Germans to

00:09:51.220 --> 00:09:53.600
travel to the Congo to purchase rubber.

00:09:53.600 --> 00:09:57.440
He was hung by The Force Republique without
receiving a trial.

00:09:57.440 --> 00:10:01.430
Germany and Britain were outraged that he
was killed without ever committing any crime.

00:10:01.430 --> 00:10:06.220
Leopold was forced to pay substantial fines
to both governments for violating the treaty,

00:10:06.220 --> 00:10:08.790
and the incident was called The Stokes Affair.

00:10:08.790 --> 00:10:12.020
However, paying this fine was just a drop
in the bucket.

00:10:12.020 --> 00:10:18.400
King Leopold II made a profit of 220 million
francs, which would be worth more than $1

00:10:18.400 --> 00:10:19.640
billion today.

00:10:19.640 --> 00:10:28.170
Exposing The Truth of Leopold’s Lies
Leopold II hired a team of propaganda writers

00:10:28.170 --> 00:10:31.350
to publish books and articles about what a
great job he was doing.

00:10:31.350 --> 00:10:35.510
None of these writers had ever actually traveled
to The Congo Free State, but they were happy

00:10:35.510 --> 00:10:38.450
to glorify their king’s Christian mission.

00:10:38.450 --> 00:10:41.740
However, journalists from Great Britain and
The United States were beginning to travel

00:10:41.740 --> 00:10:45.100
to The Congo Free State and report what they
saw.

00:10:45.100 --> 00:10:49.510
In the year 1890, an American Civil War veteran
named George Washington Williams visited The

00:10:49.510 --> 00:10:52.330
Congo Free State, and he was horrified.

00:10:52.330 --> 00:10:57.000
He wrote an open letter to King Leopold II,
recounting the horrors he witnessed while

00:10:57.000 --> 00:10:58.000
visiting the country.

00:10:58.000 --> 00:11:00.510
The King never replied.

00:11:00.510 --> 00:11:05.029
A man named Edmund Dene Morel worked as a
clerk at a shipping firm in Liverpool, England.

00:11:05.029 --> 00:11:09.180
Belgian ships would come and go delivering
rubber to Liverpool from The Congo.

00:11:09.180 --> 00:11:13.320
Murel knew that it wouldn’t be possible
for Belgium to produce such a high volume

00:11:13.320 --> 00:11:16.180
of rubber, unless they were using slave labor.

00:11:16.180 --> 00:11:20.230
He began investigating, and when he discovered
the horrors about what was actually happening,

00:11:20.230 --> 00:11:24.621
he wrote several anonymous articles for a
British newspaper called The Speaker, exposing

00:11:24.621 --> 00:11:26.540
the truth about what he saw.

00:11:26.540 --> 00:11:32.410
He wrote that this was “the greatest crime
that has ever been committed in the history

00:11:32.410 --> 00:11:33.620
of the world.”

00:11:33.620 --> 00:11:37.720
In 1901, the shipping company offered Morel
a job to manage the shipments of rubber to

00:11:37.720 --> 00:11:38.990
and from The Congo.

00:11:38.990 --> 00:11:42.870
They were willing to pay him a huge salary
in exchange for his silence.

00:11:42.870 --> 00:11:47.020
He turned it down, and became a full-time
journalist instead.

00:11:47.020 --> 00:11:50.600
He became so passionate about the cause, that
he began publishing his own newspaper called

00:11:50.600 --> 00:11:53.820
The West African Mail with any new information
he found.

00:11:53.820 --> 00:11:57.420
In 1906, he published a book called Red Rubber.

00:11:57.420 --> 00:12:00.840
Another journalist named Roger Casement was
sent to interview people of the Congo to get

00:12:00.840 --> 00:12:04.000
their testimonies about the human rights abuses
in the country.

00:12:04.000 --> 00:12:08.010
He realized that it was crucial to convincing
the white Christian missionaries to come forward

00:12:08.010 --> 00:12:11.790
with their stories, because they had been
there from the beginning, and they could prove

00:12:11.790 --> 00:12:15.560
that King Leopold II was aware of the atrocities.

00:12:15.560 --> 00:12:19.740
After Roger Casement’s report was published,
King Leopold II knew that if he did not respond

00:12:19.740 --> 00:12:22.570
with his own inquiry, this would be the end
of him.

00:12:22.570 --> 00:12:26.040
He sent his own International Commission to
the Congo, in hopes that he could bribe them.

00:12:26.040 --> 00:12:30.670
He thought that he could pay them off to publish
whatever he wanted them to say.

00:12:30.670 --> 00:12:32.040
This totally backfired.

00:12:32.040 --> 00:12:36.320
A Christian missionary named John Harris had
been living in The Congo Free State for years.

00:12:36.320 --> 00:12:39.930
He and his wife devoted their lives to helping
the Congolese people.

00:12:39.930 --> 00:12:44.470
When King Leopold’s International Commission
showed up, John Harris was ready for him.

00:12:44.470 --> 00:12:49.030
He gathered a group of Congolese people who
testified to the death, torture, mutilation,

00:12:49.030 --> 00:12:52.230
rape, and enslavement that they suffered at
the hands of King Leopold’s men.

00:12:52.230 --> 00:12:56.420
His wife, Alice Harris, was a photographer,
and she was able to present them with photographic

00:12:56.420 --> 00:12:59.600
evidence of the horrors they had seen.

00:12:59.600 --> 00:13:02.990
When the International Commission returned
to Belgium, they published a 50-page report

00:13:02.990 --> 00:13:07.470
on all of the human rights abuses they had
found in The Congo, and submitted it to King

00:13:07.470 --> 00:13:08.960
Leopold II.

00:13:08.960 --> 00:13:12.910
Once he realized that he could no longer get
away with his lies, Leopold ordered all of

00:13:12.910 --> 00:13:17.080
the Congo Free State records to be burned,
so that there would be no evidence of his

00:13:17.080 --> 00:13:18.080
crimes.

00:13:18.080 --> 00:13:22.220
In 1908, The Congo became a Belgian colony,
but they didn’t seize it from the King.

00:13:22.220 --> 00:13:25.300
Instead, they paid him 50 million francs for
the purchase.

00:13:25.300 --> 00:13:29.990
He died just one year later, in 1909.

00:13:29.990 --> 00:13:36.440
A Shocking Legacy
Once the Belgian government visited The Congo,

00:13:36.440 --> 00:13:39.339
they found far more profitable resources than
just rubber.

00:13:39.339 --> 00:13:44.100
There were diamonds, gold, and ivory that
could be sold for massive profits.

00:13:44.100 --> 00:13:48.480
The government ended slavery, and employed
the Congolese people to work for wages, instead.

00:13:48.480 --> 00:13:51.280
Very soon after, Belgium became extremely
wealthy.

00:13:51.280 --> 00:13:55.040
The city of Brussels now has some of the most
breathtaking architecture in the world, complete

00:13:55.040 --> 00:13:59.830
with golden statues of King Leopold II, all
because of the money he brought in from The

00:13:59.830 --> 00:14:00.830
Congo.

00:14:00.830 --> 00:14:05.230
But the Belgian government had to make a decision-
What do they tell the public?

00:14:05.230 --> 00:14:09.430
Leopold II had lied to his people for so long,
and they looked up to him like a father figure

00:14:09.430 --> 00:14:11.529
who brought glory to the country.

00:14:11.529 --> 00:14:15.410
Not only would the citizens be disappointed,
but it would make Belgium look terrible to

00:14:15.410 --> 00:14:16.610
the outside world.

00:14:16.610 --> 00:14:19.420
Their nation was still less than 100 years
old at the time.

00:14:19.420 --> 00:14:23.180
England and the United States had already
outlawed slavery in the 1800’s, so their

00:14:23.180 --> 00:14:28.270
short history, their king had already managed
to take steps backwards in humanitarian progress.

00:14:28.270 --> 00:14:32.170
The Belgian government chose to allow their
people to continue believing the lie that

00:14:32.170 --> 00:14:34.410
King Leopold II had built for himself.

00:14:34.410 --> 00:14:38.120
They taught their children that there never
was any slavery in The Congo Free State, and

00:14:38.120 --> 00:14:41.170
that everything King Leopold II did was wonderful.

00:14:41.170 --> 00:14:46.330
This lie was retold generation after generation,
to the point where it became their new truth,

00:14:46.330 --> 00:14:48.070
and part of their cultural identity.

00:14:48.070 --> 00:14:54.149
Before his death, in 1897, Leopold II created
a human zoo at his summer estate.

00:14:54.149 --> 00:14:59.260
He built a model African village and captured
267 Congolese people to live there.

00:14:59.260 --> 00:15:03.710
Belgian people showed up to gawk at them,
throwing peanuts and bananas over the fence,

00:15:03.710 --> 00:15:05.300
as if they were monkeys.

00:15:05.300 --> 00:15:09.250
They were forced to stay outdoors in these
village in all kinds of weather.

00:15:09.250 --> 00:15:12.400
Seven of those people died of influenza and
pneumonia.

00:15:12.400 --> 00:15:15.940
After he died, the king’s estate became
The Royal Museum of Central Africa, and it

00:15:15.940 --> 00:15:20.280
continued to glorify Leopold II’s achievements
in colonization.

00:15:20.280 --> 00:15:24.880
Decades after his death, in 1958, the government
of Belgium even went so far as to replicate

00:15:24.880 --> 00:15:30.649
his human zoo at the Brussels World Fair,
putting Congolese people on display like animals

00:15:30.649 --> 00:15:31.690
once again.

00:15:31.690 --> 00:15:36.900
Nearly every western nation has some history
of slavery and genocide, but in most Belgian

00:15:36.900 --> 00:15:40.360
classes, they will never hear the truth about
King Leopold II.

00:15:40.360 --> 00:15:43.630
They will say that slavery never happened
in The Congo.

00:15:43.630 --> 00:15:47.300
Since the records were destroyed, we will
never know just how many people Leopold was

00:15:47.300 --> 00:15:48.760
responsible for killing.

00:15:48.760 --> 00:15:54.080
Some estimate that it is roughly 4 million,
while others believe it is as high as 10 million.

00:15:54.080 --> 00:15:59.500
Somewhere between 70 to 90% of the total population
was wiped out.

00:15:59.500 --> 00:16:02.910
In the age of the internet, it has become
much more difficult for Belgium to ignore

00:16:02.910 --> 00:16:04.410
the reality of what happened.

00:16:04.410 --> 00:16:09.399
In 2018, the curators of the Royal Museum
of Central Africa finally decided to change

00:16:09.399 --> 00:16:13.520
the exhibits to honor the lives lost by the
native Congolese people.

00:16:13.520 --> 00:16:17.390
However, Congolese people who visited the
exhibit said that it’s still not enough,

00:16:17.390 --> 00:16:21.710
and that as long as the story is told from
the perspective of a white Belgian person,

00:16:21.710 --> 00:16:39.170
the country will never show the full truth
about the monstrous deeds

00:16:39.170 --> 00:16:56.670
of

00:16:56.670 --> 00:17:45.969
King Leopold II.

